{"name":"Antarctic Love","hex":"#eddee6","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"antarctic","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Alternative spelling of Antarctic."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/antarctic"},{"term":"love","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A deep caring for the existence of another.","Strong affection."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To have a strong affection for (someone or something).","To need, thrive on."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/love"}],"entries":[{"title":"Antarctic","blocks":[{"text":"The Antarctic is the polar region of Earth that surrounds the South Pole, lying within the Antarctic Circle. It is diametrically opposite of the Arctic region around the North Pole."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/74/Antarctic-Overview-Map-EN.tif/lossless-page1-330px-Antarctic-Overview-Map-EN.tif.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Antarctic","wikidata":"Q1555938"},{"title":"Love","blocks":[{"text":"Love encompasses a range of strong and positive emotional and mental states, from the most sublime virtue or good habit, the deepest interpersonal affection, to the simplest pleasure. An example of this range of meanings is that the love of a mother differs from the love of a spouse, which differs from the love for food. Most commonly, love refers to a feeling of strong attraction and emotional attachment."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Love","wikidata":"Q316"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/14/AntarcticPlate.png/500px-AntarcticPlate.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/14/AntarcticPlate.png/1280px-AntarcticPlate.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/w